# fixtures/lq/cases/envelope.cases: result-envelope goldens of [LQ/envelope] and [F19] (WP-22, R-FIX).
# A result case states one result (the note and the '%% nodes' block, one node object of [LQ/envelope §7.4] per
# line, give the store facts its rows need) and asserts both renderings: '%% text' (the text result, each line
# ended by LF) and '%% json' (the --json v1 envelope, one line). The values inside 'budget' are inputs, not derived:
# a harness checks the budget object's keys and their order, not its values (INDEX.md §4 G-12).
# Header, footer and TX cases assert text lines only. Commit ids are synthetic: c + the SHA-256 of a label.
# Goldens are authored from the specification text, never copied from [50 §2.9]'s examples (review S-24); where
# they differ from an example, the note says why.
# Format: fixtures/lq/INDEX.md §2.

%% case result-node-one-row
%% source [LQ/envelope §3]
%% source §5.3
%% source §7
%% source [50 §2.9] Q1
%% note MATCH (t {id: #51}) RETURN t on main at rev 4480 (a tip view): one node row.
%% text
branch: main | rev 4480 | 1 row
#51 task open P1 "Wire lease reclaim" parent:#9 blockers:#12,#17 inherited:#7 BLOCKED
